### Six new-page proposals — your decision

**1. `ingredients/cereals` — 8 sources** (altunay2023, codex-cccf17-2024, codex-cxs-193-1995, efsa-cadmium-contam-2009, efsa-lead-contam-2010, efsa-nickel-contam-2020, jecfa-73rd-cadmium-2010, nordberg2015)

All Codex/EFSA/JECFA regulatory sources that classify grains using the standard food-law category "cereals" — which includes wheat, barley, rye, oats, maize, and rice together. Can't redirect to `non-rice-grains.md` (rice is a cereal grain; these sources cover it). Would anchor the regulation pages correctly against Codex taxonomy.

